# Server action errors

## Rule

Server actions and route handlers that return errors to the client **must not** return user-facing English strings. Return a **code only**:

```ts
import { fail, logActionFailure } from "@repo/utils/action-error";

if (!user) return fail("UNAUTHORIZED");

try {
  // ...
} catch (err) {
  logActionFailure("saveLoyaltyCard", err);
  return fail("LOYALTY_CARD_SAVE_FAILED");
}
```

## Error codes

- Use **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE** (e.g. `BUSINESS_NOT_FOUND`, `STAMP_EXPIRED`).
- Add the code to `ActionErrorCode` in `packages/utils/src/action-error.ts`.
- Add translated copy under `errors.actions.<CODE>` in `apps/<app>/messages/en.json`.
- Never expose Supabase/Postgres raw messages to the UI — log server-side with `logActionFailure`.

## Client display

In client components, resolve codes with `resolveActionError`:

```tsx
const tErrors = useTranslations("errors.actions");
// ...
if (result.error) setError(resolveActionError(tErrors, result.error));
```

For React Query / thrown errors, resolve inside the hook with the same helper.

## Success feedback

After a successful mutation (save, approve, switch context, etc.), show a **translated toast** so users get clear confirmation — especially when the UI refreshes or the item disappears from the list.

```tsx
import { showActionSuccess } from "@/shared/utils/action-feedback";

const t = useTranslations("loyaltyCard");
// ...
if (!result.error) {
  showActionSuccess(t, "success.saved");
  router.refresh();
}
```

- Add copy under `<feature>.success.*` in `apps/<app>/messages/en.json` (same namespace as the feature UI).
- Use `{customer}`, `{branch}`, `{business}`, `{card}`, etc. in message strings and pass matching values to `showActionSuccess`.
- Use `showActionSuccess` from `@/shared/utils/action-feedback` (wraps Sonner; `Toaster` is in the app root layout).
- Redirect-on-success flows (sign-in, add business) do not need a toast — navigation is the feedback.

## Warnings (non-fatal)

Partial success may return `{ warning: { code: "DEMO_NO_REDEMPTION_CODE" } }`. Resolve with `resolveActionWarning` (merchant) or the same `errors.actions` namespace.

## Types

- Use `ActionResult<T>` from `@/shared/types/action-result` (merchant) or import from `@repo/utils/action-error` (admin).
- Do not use `{ error?: string }`.
